WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.040
Dear Jesus, may I enter into the eternal divine order of God to place my absolute nothingness

2
00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:14.200
in the heart of the most holy trinity, to give to my God the joy of fulfilling the purpose

3
00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:19.980
of my existence by doing all the acts of my life through the immaculate heart of my mother

4
00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:27.600
Mary and in the divine will of God, and in this same manner may I live, pray, act, eat,

5
00:00:27.600 --> 00:00:34.640
walk, sleep and do everything, may my soul be devoid of any other longings wants or desires,

6
00:00:34.640 --> 00:00:41.380
and may you my beloved divine will do with me whatever you want or desire, all I ask

7
00:00:41.380 --> 00:00:47.120
is that you bind me to your most holy will so intimately that I may never swear from

8
00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:53.160
carrying out what I know to be your good pleasure, and that I remain so docile to the movements

9
00:00:53.160 --> 00:00:59.580
of your divine will that you never perceive even a breath of resistance in my soul to your

10
00:00:59.580 --> 00:01:05.260
requests of me come divine will with all the angels and saints, especially my sweet mother

11
00:01:05.260 --> 00:01:12.380
Mary to touch my forehead to imprint on it the Holy Spirit and infuse in me true light,

12
00:01:12.380 --> 00:01:17.760
so that I may understand the truths and the good that are in these writings and prayers.

13
00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:18.760
Amen.

14
00:01:18.760 --> 00:01:24.880
As a melda said, we're beginning on October the 13th 1926, and we have some absolutely

15
00:01:24.880 --> 00:01:28.280
wonderful messages for us this evening.

16
00:01:28.280 --> 00:01:33.400
So the first thing we're going to deal with is that the Lord wants to turn our acts into

17
00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:37.560
light and therefore to divinise them.

18
00:01:37.560 --> 00:01:43.400
I was fusing all of myself in the Holy Divine volition, Louisa said, and while I was going

19
00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:50.040
around in it in the divine will doing my acts, my beloved Jesus moved in my interior and told

20
00:01:50.040 --> 00:02:00.800
me, my daughter, each act, watch this now, each prayer and each pain which the soul makes

21
00:02:00.800 --> 00:02:05.720
enter into the light of my will actually becomes light.

22
00:02:05.720 --> 00:02:12.800
Now we know that God is light, that's one time on five, God is light.

23
00:02:12.800 --> 00:02:19.400
So in other words, everything we put into the divine will becomes divinised and it forms

24
00:02:19.400 --> 00:02:24.480
one more ray in the sun of the eternal volition.

25
00:02:24.480 --> 00:02:28.480
We put one tiny ray into that eternal light.

26
00:02:28.480 --> 00:02:30.080
It's an incredible thing.

27
00:02:30.080 --> 00:02:33.480
Everything that are in these messages tonight are so incredible that you really want to

28
00:02:33.480 --> 00:02:36.240
spend the whole time on one line, you know.

29
00:02:36.240 --> 00:02:42.240
These rays, in other words, are acts turned into light, form the most beautiful glory

30
00:02:42.240 --> 00:02:46.760
that the soul can give to the eternal Fiat.

31
00:02:46.760 --> 00:02:48.160
How do you give glory to God?

32
00:02:48.160 --> 00:02:51.680
Well, you've just been told, it's absolutely incredible.

33
00:02:51.680 --> 00:02:59.000
So these acts turned into light become rays in the sun of the eternal volition and they

34
00:02:59.000 --> 00:03:04.360
form the most beautiful glory that the soul can give to the divine Fiat in such a way

35
00:03:04.360 --> 00:03:12.840
that seeing itself so glorified by its own light, it invests these rays with new knowledge.

36
00:03:12.840 --> 00:03:16.880
Now, there's going to be a good bit about knowledge in these writings.

37
00:03:16.880 --> 00:03:19.760
We cannot use the word knowledge in English.

38
00:03:19.760 --> 00:03:21.720
The word knowledge is plural.

39
00:03:21.720 --> 00:03:26.240
So I have to change the sentence to make it sound proper in English.

40
00:03:26.240 --> 00:03:32.520
So the divine will invest these rays with new knowledge, which converting into voices

41
00:03:32.520 --> 00:03:38.720
or messages that we understand, that we can hear, they manifest to the soul more surprises

42
00:03:38.720 --> 00:03:40.960
about my will.

43
00:03:40.960 --> 00:03:47.240
Put very, very simply, the more we put into the divine will, the more we understand.

44
00:03:47.240 --> 00:03:53.360
The less we put into the divine will, the less we understand because when these rays

45
00:03:53.360 --> 00:03:59.520
are put into the divine will, then knowledge is communicated to us.

46
00:03:59.520 --> 00:04:03.360
And converting into voices, that means something you can actually hear.

47
00:04:03.360 --> 00:04:07.920
We learn more and more about the divine will and as we know, having gone through so much

48
00:04:07.920 --> 00:04:12.400
of these volumes, there's just more and more and more.

49
00:04:12.400 --> 00:04:19.520
But do you know what this knowledge of mine actually does or forms in the soul?

50
00:04:19.520 --> 00:04:23.720
This knowledge forms the e-clips of the human will.

51
00:04:23.720 --> 00:04:28.200
Here you got the answer to questions that will be asked in the early volumes.

52
00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:32.720
In other words, how can you put aside the human will?

53
00:04:32.720 --> 00:04:40.240
And the human will has got to be pushed aside simply by the sheer light of the divine will

54
00:04:40.240 --> 00:04:45.160
and the understanding that comes with this knowledge that's given to us with every single

55
00:04:45.160 --> 00:04:46.920
act that we do.

56
00:04:46.920 --> 00:04:54.120
The human will is just shown exactly that it cannot be the dominator in us.

57
00:04:54.120 --> 00:04:55.280
And so it becomes e-clipsed.

58
00:04:55.280 --> 00:05:00.280
Now, he's going to explain this in terms of stars in the sky in a minute.

59
00:05:00.280 --> 00:05:06.640
The stronger the light is, the more the rays there are and the more strongly the human will

60
00:05:06.640 --> 00:05:09.280
becomes dazzled and e-clipsed.

61
00:05:09.280 --> 00:05:14.680
So the light becomes stronger as you put more rays in, that means you do more acts.

62
00:05:14.680 --> 00:05:19.680
And as the light becomes stronger, then the human will becomes more and more dazzled and

63
00:05:19.680 --> 00:05:20.680
e-clipsed.

64
00:05:20.680 --> 00:05:24.160
In other words, this is really under our control.

65
00:05:24.160 --> 00:05:28.480
If I don't bother to do any acts, if I don't bother to put anything into the divine will,

66
00:05:28.480 --> 00:05:34.020
I'm not putting in my penny's worth into this to give God a chance to do anything.

67
00:05:34.020 --> 00:05:35.960
I'm not giving him anything.

68
00:05:35.960 --> 00:05:41.760
You remember the feeding of the 5,000, Jesus expected someone to give him bread.

69
00:05:41.760 --> 00:05:45.000
Someone had to do it, but only a child in the crowd understood.

70
00:05:45.000 --> 00:05:49.640
The man wants bread, I only have these tiny little loaves, I'll give him this.

71
00:05:49.640 --> 00:05:55.600
With Eucharist every day, we have to give him something, we give him the little tiny wafers,

72
00:05:55.600 --> 00:05:58.800
we give him the tiny drop of wine, we give him something to work with.

73
00:05:58.800 --> 00:06:00.520
It's not magic.

74
00:06:00.520 --> 00:06:05.600
In the divine will, we have to give him our acts and the more we do it, the greater the

75
00:06:05.600 --> 00:06:07.160
effect.

76
00:06:07.160 --> 00:06:12.560
So this happens in such a way that the human will almost feels impotent to act.

77
00:06:12.560 --> 00:06:14.840
I love the word almost.

78
00:06:14.840 --> 00:06:19.080
That's the kind of word you need to underline because he's going to tell us and he will

79
00:06:19.080 --> 00:06:20.680
repeat it over and over.

80
00:06:20.680 --> 00:06:24.680
He never takes our free will from us, ever.

81
00:06:24.680 --> 00:06:30.180
He's going to explain that the reason why the human will becomes almost impotent is

82
00:06:30.180 --> 00:06:36.880
that it is so occupied in feeding the divine will with its acts, in other words, we choose

83
00:06:36.880 --> 00:06:39.720
to do our acts in the divine will.

84
00:06:39.720 --> 00:06:44.720
So the human will is almost impotent to act and it gives the field, in other words, we

85
00:06:44.720 --> 00:06:48.800
give the Lord the space to work for the light of the divine will.

86
00:06:48.800 --> 00:06:53.960
The human will remains occupied within the action of my will.

87
00:06:53.960 --> 00:07:01.320
Now, if you remember earlier messages in volumes 19 and 20, we were told that the way the dwellers

88
00:07:01.320 --> 00:07:07.360
of heaven live is they have their free will, but their free will is completely occupied

89
00:07:07.360 --> 00:07:09.440
in doing the divine will.

90
00:07:09.440 --> 00:07:14.380
They've made their final eternal decision about it and therefore in the same position

91
00:07:14.380 --> 00:07:19.640
as the angels now who made a final decision to enter into the divine will.

92
00:07:19.640 --> 00:07:26.280
But here on earth, they prodigy is that the more we do acts in the divine will, the more

93
00:07:26.280 --> 00:07:32.160
our human will remains occupied within the divine will and therefore we are actually

94
00:07:32.160 --> 00:07:35.680
living a heavenly life on earth.

95
00:07:35.680 --> 00:07:41.400
And just as the dwellers in heaven, the human will lacks the time, the place to operate independently

96
00:07:41.400 --> 00:07:42.400
of that.

97
00:07:42.400 --> 00:07:46.560
We use our free will to choose God.

98
00:07:46.560 --> 00:07:51.840
So in the next paragraph, then we're going to answer the question, how can this come

99
00:07:51.840 --> 00:07:54.080
about and how much do you want this?

100
00:07:54.080 --> 00:07:55.640
How much heaven do you want?

101
00:07:55.640 --> 00:07:57.240
How much happiness do you want?

102
00:07:57.240 --> 00:08:00.560
As I've said to you already, it's up to us.

103
00:08:00.560 --> 00:08:02.280
So I give you two answers.

104
00:08:02.280 --> 00:08:04.560
We have to become like the saints.

105
00:08:04.560 --> 00:08:06.520
I want to see God.

106
00:08:06.520 --> 00:08:13.320
And for that, I want to give you Exodus 33, 18 where Moses said, Lord, I need to see you.

107
00:08:13.320 --> 00:08:14.320
Show me your face.

108
00:08:14.320 --> 00:08:16.040
I actually need to see you.

109
00:08:16.040 --> 00:08:17.280
And it was not the right time.

110
00:08:17.280 --> 00:08:20.320
So he wasn't allowed, but we can see him.

111
00:08:20.320 --> 00:08:21.680
It's absolutely incredible.

112
00:08:21.680 --> 00:08:26.080
Every time you look at the Holy Eucharist, you're seeing God.

113
00:08:26.080 --> 00:08:27.440
Okay.

114
00:08:27.440 --> 00:08:34.440
As we enter more and more deeply into the divine will and the human will is quietly eclipsed

115
00:08:34.440 --> 00:08:37.280
and put aside and the divine will takes over.

116
00:08:37.280 --> 00:08:41.240
We actually see God more and more and more.

117
00:08:41.240 --> 00:08:46.840
You already know him better than 99.9% of humanity.

118
00:08:46.840 --> 00:08:49.480
You already know him better than that.

119
00:08:49.480 --> 00:08:54.760
Now we can go forward and we can live the life of heaven on earth to the extent that

120
00:08:54.760 --> 00:08:56.040
we want to do it.

121
00:08:56.040 --> 00:08:57.040
Okay.

122
00:08:57.040 --> 00:09:02.920
So he gives an example, it's like the human eye when it stares at the sun.

123
00:09:02.920 --> 00:09:07.300
So the human eye now is the human will and the sun is therefore the divine will.

124
00:09:07.300 --> 00:09:10.760
The strength of the light invests the pupil and lording over it.

125
00:09:10.760 --> 00:09:13.880
It renders as impotent to look at anything else.

126
00:09:13.880 --> 00:09:17.280
But in spite of this, the eye has not lost its vision.

127
00:09:17.280 --> 00:09:21.200
It is the strength of the light that is overpowered.

128
00:09:21.200 --> 00:09:26.520
It takes away any other object from the one who looks at us and allows him only to look

129
00:09:26.520 --> 00:09:27.520
at the light.

130
00:09:27.520 --> 00:09:30.520
That's what you call the eclipsing of one with the other.

131
00:09:30.520 --> 00:09:35.400
I will never take away free will from the human will.

132
00:09:35.400 --> 00:09:38.720
It's an extremely important statement.

133
00:09:38.720 --> 00:09:40.120
You can't say free willing.

134
00:09:40.120 --> 00:09:41.120
That's not English.

135
00:09:41.120 --> 00:09:44.080
I will never take free will away from the human will.

136
00:09:44.080 --> 00:09:51.280
This is a great gift that was given to man in creating him and which makes them, that

137
00:09:51.280 --> 00:09:58.160
is man or humanity, distinguishable as to whether they want to be my true children or

138
00:09:58.160 --> 00:09:59.400
not.

139
00:09:59.400 --> 00:10:02.120
This is an extremely important statement.

140
00:10:02.120 --> 00:10:08.160
I just said it's entirely up to us whether we enter into the divine will or not, whether

141
00:10:08.160 --> 00:10:12.520
we do the acts, whether we multiply them, whether we truly want to see God, whether

142
00:10:12.520 --> 00:10:15.680
we want heaven and that's entirely up to us.

143
00:10:15.680 --> 00:10:21.520
But whether they want to be my true children or not, Jesus has told us many parables in

144
00:10:21.520 --> 00:10:28.680
which just to take one example that in the end the wheat will be separated from the chaff.

145
00:10:28.680 --> 00:10:33.320
The good fish, the bad fish, the sheep, the goat, the ones who want to be his true children

146
00:10:33.320 --> 00:10:34.320
or not.

147
00:10:34.320 --> 00:10:36.120
Now, who are the true children?

148
00:10:36.120 --> 00:10:38.080
That's the Romans 819.

149
00:10:38.080 --> 00:10:42.960
The true children are the ones living in the divine will and then some people who are good

150
00:10:42.960 --> 00:10:49.600
people and who are prepared to have a relationship with God but not go this far.

151
00:10:49.600 --> 00:10:51.920
They'll decide they're not taking this.

152
00:10:51.920 --> 00:10:59.880
So the separation takes place on the earth and the separation takes place among us very

153
00:10:59.880 --> 00:11:03.760
quietly in the hearts of each one of us.

154
00:11:03.760 --> 00:11:09.680
Then he says, "But rather with the light of the knowledge about my will, I will form

155
00:11:09.680 --> 00:11:16.200
more than solar rays and whoever wants to know them and look at them will be invested

156
00:11:16.200 --> 00:11:17.200
by this light."

157
00:11:17.200 --> 00:11:23.000
So if you want to be one of the true children, yes, he will absolutely flood us with his

158
00:11:23.000 --> 00:11:25.640
light to the extent that we actually want.

159
00:11:25.640 --> 00:11:32.240
So they will be invested by this light in such a way that eclipsed the human will, will

160
00:11:32.240 --> 00:11:36.880
take delight and love looking at this light.

161
00:11:36.880 --> 00:11:44.120
Now looking at this light, what we were talking about is that to truly become a person living

162
00:11:44.120 --> 00:11:50.380
in the divine will, you have to become a contemplative.

163
00:11:50.380 --> 00:11:55.520
I have contested a point from the very beginning of my contact with the divine will.

164
00:11:55.520 --> 00:11:59.160
The impression that was given to me at the beginning is you had to say multitudes of

165
00:11:59.160 --> 00:12:08.200
prayers and you look at Louisa and she was a very deep, exalted contemplative.

166
00:12:08.200 --> 00:12:10.400
It's the contemplation, it's the secret.

167
00:12:10.400 --> 00:12:13.520
It's in contemplation that you come to see God.

168
00:12:13.520 --> 00:12:18.240
It's in contemplation that you reach out and you actually take possession.

169
00:12:18.240 --> 00:12:24.560
And the Lord has been talking about this for many, many volumes at this particular point.

170
00:12:24.560 --> 00:12:31.800
So 2 Corinthians 3, 18, St Paul says that we become like that which we worship.

171
00:12:31.800 --> 00:12:37.600
Hence in the recent retreat, I challenged the group who came on retreat with me to prostrate

172
00:12:37.600 --> 00:12:39.880
before the Lord during the night.

173
00:12:39.880 --> 00:12:44.480
The night is a very wonderful time for contemplation because all the distractions of the day are

174
00:12:44.480 --> 00:12:46.920
taken away.

175
00:12:46.920 --> 00:12:52.400
And they're lying on the floor before the living God, that's where miracles happen.

176
00:12:52.400 --> 00:12:57.520
And the one who gave me the headline for this, you might be surprised to hear, was John Paul

177
00:12:57.520 --> 00:12:58.520
II.

178
00:12:58.520 --> 00:13:04.960
Pope John Paul II used to prostrate before the Blessed Sacrament every night for at least

179
00:13:04.960 --> 00:13:08.360
an hour or two, no matter where he was on the earth.

180
00:13:08.360 --> 00:13:14.160
That was his giving of himself to God and his listening to God for what God wanted him

181
00:13:14.160 --> 00:13:16.280
to do and look what he did.

182
00:13:16.280 --> 00:13:17.280
So that's it.

183
00:13:17.280 --> 00:13:22.520
We have to become contemplative because that's where you see and you hear.

184
00:13:22.520 --> 00:13:24.760
That's where you reach out and you take possession.

185
00:13:24.760 --> 00:13:25.760
Okay.

186
00:13:25.760 --> 00:13:28.440
That's where you become invested with the light.

187
00:13:28.440 --> 00:13:34.000
So the human will will take the light and love looking at this light, that's contemplation

188
00:13:34.000 --> 00:13:39.320
and will feel fortunate that the action of the light takes place of its own.

189
00:13:39.320 --> 00:13:45.240
So we feel very fortunate that God decides to actually work with us with the small little

190
00:13:45.240 --> 00:13:47.400
creatures that we are.

191
00:13:47.400 --> 00:13:50.800
And it will lose love and delight for other things.

192
00:13:50.800 --> 00:13:55.800
Now there's one of the keys to check how much progress we're making in the divine will

193
00:13:55.800 --> 00:14:03.000
because if we're not moving away from material things and useless things and distractions

194
00:14:03.000 --> 00:14:06.640
and all the rest of it, then we're not moving forward.

195
00:14:06.640 --> 00:14:11.440
You know that if an aircraft is going to take to the sky, it has to leave the earth behind

196
00:14:11.440 --> 00:14:12.440
it.

197
00:14:12.440 --> 00:14:15.440
It has to take to the lonely looking sky.

198
00:14:15.440 --> 00:14:19.720
You can't actually bring the country with you, you've got to leave it behind.

199
00:14:19.720 --> 00:14:25.960
And so when we make a decision that we really, really want to see God, we have to let the

200
00:14:25.960 --> 00:14:29.120
earthly things fall back as well.

201
00:14:29.120 --> 00:14:35.440
So this is why he said, "I'm saying so much about my will to form this strong light."

202
00:14:35.440 --> 00:14:41.040
Because the stronger the light is, the greater is the eclipse that it forms in order to occupy

203
00:14:41.040 --> 00:14:42.840
the human will.

204
00:14:42.840 --> 00:14:43.840
Okay.

205
00:14:43.840 --> 00:14:47.080
So God doesn't destroy our human will as he said himself.

206
00:14:47.080 --> 00:14:49.400
He occupies it with the divine will.

207
00:14:49.400 --> 00:14:53.200
I'm not an unspeakable privilege, that actually is.

208
00:14:53.200 --> 00:14:54.200
Okay.

209
00:14:54.200 --> 00:15:02.760
So in this contemplation, we are drawn upwards towards God and he descends downwards towards

210
00:15:02.760 --> 00:15:05.160
us.

211
00:15:05.160 --> 00:15:11.480
And we have this extraordinary meeting, as Saint Paul says, in the air, that means entirely

212
00:15:11.480 --> 00:15:18.200
in the spiritual sphere, not in the physical, not in the material, in the region where spirit

213
00:15:18.200 --> 00:15:20.360
actually exists.

214
00:15:20.360 --> 00:15:24.480
So he gives an example now of the sky, which he likes doing.

215
00:15:24.480 --> 00:15:27.920
Look at the sky, he said, "This is an image of what we're talking about.

216
00:15:27.920 --> 00:15:32.080
If you look at us at night, you will see the sky studded with stars.

217
00:15:32.080 --> 00:15:36.080
But if you look at it during the day, the stars are no longer exists for the human eye,

218
00:15:36.080 --> 00:15:37.600
and others you can't see them.

219
00:15:37.600 --> 00:15:40.080
However, they're still there.

220
00:15:40.080 --> 00:15:43.880
The fact that you can't see them doesn't mean that they're not there.

221
00:15:43.880 --> 00:15:47.920
They're still in their place in the sky, just as they are at night.

222
00:15:47.920 --> 00:15:52.440
But who has had the strength to make the stars disappear, though they are present in this

223
00:15:52.440 --> 00:15:53.440
full daylight?

224
00:15:53.440 --> 00:15:56.040
It is the power of the sun.

225
00:15:56.040 --> 00:16:00.920
You see, the sun is the light eclipsing them, the lesser light.

226
00:16:00.920 --> 00:16:08.080
So the divine will is the great light that eclipses our human will as we allow it to

227
00:16:08.080 --> 00:16:12.240
shine fully on us in contemplation.

228
00:16:12.240 --> 00:16:17.640
